aving been vaccinated  what's going to happen  no in the short term there'll be some  staggering of start times and staggering  of leave times  there may in some place not be intervals  but no  no need for testing to take place and  stuff the good news is  because of the huge sacrifices  everyone's made across the country  we're making really good progress on the  virus going down the yard number  continues to  be doing well the vaccine roller  continues to go well  everyone should regularly test you can  now get free test kits  from your pharmacy or by going to the  relevant  web page it's really important we  continue to make progress  follow the advice that we're given the  prime minister's announcement today will  continue to bode well  for us to finally come out of this on  the 21st of june properly  but it's going to be great summer it's  going to be a great summer in london so  the fact you can't go overseas don't  worry you can come to  london and that's what let's do london  is all about  and uh there's talk about bringing the  big british-only  european football final to uh london  rather than holding it in turkey  are you involved in those discussions  and will you able be able to give uae  for the sort of wave as it wants  absolutely we've been speaking to the fa  and uaf we've got great relations with  uefa and the fa because of  our work with the euro 2020s which has  been delayed by year  we're ready and waiting for me doesn't  make sense for  chelsea fans man city fans to travel to  a red list country they shouldn't be  traveling but also rather than  there being an empty stadium we could  have thousands of fans safely watching  the team they love  this would be historic champion league  final city versus chelsea  city of uh could potentially win their  first champions league at chelsea their  second one  it's going to be a great game even  better if it's taking place in london  now let's talk about the labour party  what do you make of the way shakir  stammer has  handled the poor results obviously  outside london  for the labour party  i think the results were mixed across  the country we did well in london  in manchester in liverpool in wells  really good to see dan norris a friend  when i used to be an mp being elected  for the west of england the first time  we've won that seat  really could see us gaining a seat from  the tories in cambridge and peterborough  those mural elections really great to  see tracy brabin  the first ever mayor of west yorkshire  relieved  to finally stop seeing a decline of our  party in scotland but clearly  they were mixed and i think cair's right  to accelerate the progress we've got to  make  to win back the trust and confidence of  voters across the country his right to  do so he's our leader  and he should be supported in making  those changes i'm really pleased  that kear's not happy with the results  because they were a mixed bag  but demoting prominent women demoting  angela rainer demoting and lisa dodds  is that the right message  well hold on a sec angela rainer is one  of the best politicians we have she  needs to be speaking to the public  far more than she does as party chair  she's been brilliant on my campaign  uh my frustration is because she's part  of chair trying to sort out a party  she's not been doing more of that so i  think kei's right to get it in the front  speaking to listening and engaging with  voters she's brilliant  and rachel reeves will be the new shadow  chancellor  again she'll be able to use her  experience as a long-standing mp but  also anna lee is able to use her skills  as the as party cheers so it's really  good and also shabana  mahmoud a birmingham mp really good  experience  taking over the the party chair roller  as well so look i think there's an  exciting team that  that kier's got around him helping look  politics is a team sport  and those of us who are labor are on the  same side but we've got to realize  that tribal politics is